				}
			]
			rewards: [{
				id: "6EDF60D97C8BD59B"
				type: "choice"
				table_id: 2640422954496342337L
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "Going Up"
			x: -3.5d
			y: 0.25d
			shape: "square"
			subtitle: "MOD : Elevator Mod"
			description: [
				"&eBeing able to make large bases without worrying about architectual concerns like support pillars, etc can make for some fantastic designs...."
				""
				"&eBut it also can make it quite difficult to design staircases that go to all the floors that also look nice... or that don't take lots of room themselves."
				""
				"&eEnter the handy dandy magical Elevator. By placing one of these down, then another above or below it at any distance (even with blocks in between them!), you can teleport between them just by Jumping or Sneaking."
				""
				"&eYou can even Right Click the Elevator with an empty hand to configure which way you face when you teleport to that Elevator. Then you can Right Click any block onto the Elevator to disguise it."
			]
			hide_dependency_lines: true
			dependencies: ["06FED1C3C1EA8361"]
			id: "346A39F3E5E0AA7D"
			tasks: [{
				id: "25B8696EA20DC1E4"
				type: "item"
				title: "Any Color Elevator"
				item: {
					id: "itemfilters:tag"
					Count: 1b
					tag: {
						value: "elevatorid:elevators"
					}
				}
			}]
			rewards: [{
				id: "795CB37E26218E27"
				type: "choice"
				table_id: 2640422954496342337L
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "Framed in Style"
			x: -6.25d
			y: 1.25d
			shape: "square"
			subtitle: "MOD : FramedBlocks"
			description: [
				"&eNow, most blocks in the FOPGame Server only have a couple of shapes (if you are lucky). Block, stairs, slab. If its wood, it probably has a Door, Trap Door, and maybe Fences and Fence Gates. But not all the time, right?"
				""
				"&eSo instead of bothering with making versions for each Block material, a brand was introduced to cover missing shapes, and add new shapes to build with : Framed Blocks."
				""
				"&eStarting with the Framed Block, you can use it to build a quick structure. Then, you take a solid block, like say Bricks, and Right Click it onto a bare Framed Block to 'camo' it as that block. Want it to make light? Right Click some Glowstone Dust onto it too."
				""
				"&eYou can take a Framed Hammer and Right Click the Framed Block to remove the Camo."
			]
			hide_dependency_lines: true
			dependencies: ["06FED1C3C1EA8361"]
			id: "5BA547287C13B0F1"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "626AAEB10DF61FC1"
					type: "item"
					item: "framedblocks:framed_cube"
				}
				{
					id: "5F48BF8DB0451E4B"
					type: "item"
					item: "framedblocks:framed_hammer"
				}
			]
			rewards: [{
				id: "355F56A6740B6FC6"
				type: "choice"
				table_id: 2640422954496342337L
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "Framing Better"
			x: -7.25d
			y: 0.75d
			shape: "rsquare"
			description: [
				"&eFramed Blocks come in many shapes, and many of them can be rotated all around to fit into your builds."
				""
				"&eYou can use a Framed Wrench (or most any useable Wrench) to cycle through the styles and directions a Framed Block has. "
				""
				"&eAnother useful tool is the Framed Blueprint. You can Sneak + Right Click it onto a customized Frame Block to copy it. Then, as long as you have the parts in your inventory (the Framed Block, the Block using as Camo, etc), you can use the Blueprint to instantly place down more copies of it!"
			]
			dependencies: ["5BA547287C13B0F1"]
			id: "1EBB7D36D3AE7C34"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "54AEFF1FF6E68CAC"
					type: "item"
					item: "framedblocks:framed_wrench"
				}
				{
					id: "5EBB7B238FF62967"
					type: "item"
					item: {
						id: "framedblocks:framed_blueprint"
						Count: 1b
						tag: {
							blueprint_data: { }
						}
					}
				}
			]
			rewards: [{
				id: "01D6CCB2B87A3B18"
				type: "choice"
				table_id: 2640422954496342337L
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "Special Blocks"
			x: -7.25d
			y: 1.75d
			shape: "rsquare"
			description: [
				"&eAlong with a wide variety of slopes, stairs, and other shaped Framed Blocks, you can also make a few interesting ones!"
				""
				"&eThe Collapsable Framed Block lets you adjust the height of each corner with a Framed Hammer. Left Click a corner to lower it, and Sneak + Left Click to raise it."
				""
				"&eThe Framed Secret Storage is a good way to hide some useful stuff, or turn whole walls into hidden storage to keep your deco nice and tidy."
				""
				"&eThe Framed Bouncy Cube acts sort of like a Slime Block. Jumping on it makes you bounce up!"
			]
			dependencies: ["1EBB7D36D3AE7C34"]
			id: "22109511478BB0A6"
			tasks: [
